<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Harry Shepard Knapp</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1856">1856</a>–<a href="/years/1923">1923</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Harry Shepard Knapp was an officer of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states-navy">United States Navy</a> who proclaimed the American military government of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-republic">Dominican Republic</a> in November 1916, after the Dominican congress refused American demands for control of the country's finances and army. He served as military governor until 1918, ruling by decree and suspending the Dominican congress. He later commanded American naval forces in European waters during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/harry-shepard-knapp.jpg" alt="Harry Shepard Knapp" width="320" height="416" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Harry_Shepard_Knapp_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
